# EXPORT_SCOPE -- DispatchOS customer deliverable
#
# Consumed by tools/export_snapshot.sh (A-2). Allow-list: a path absent from this file
# cannot leave the box, and nothing here is exported until an export is separately
# authorized. Authorized 2026-09-02 as Option B: the customer-facing page plus the
# application source that is specifically this application's.
#
# ## What is deliberately NOT here
#
# apps/accounts -- SHARED PLATFORM SOURCE. Category 2, ruled 2026-09-02 and NOT authorized
# for inclusion. store.py imports password primitives from it and authz.py consults it for
# entitlement, but "imported by the application" is not "owned by the application": it is
# named in the architecture as a shared consumed service and has more than one consumer.
#
# RECORDED CONSEQUENCE: the authorized source export references shared platform
# functionality that is not itself included in the customer export. The exported source is
# therefore NOT a self-contained or independently buildable distribution, and it is not
# meant to be. Option B is "page + application-specific source", not "whatever makes the
# result run".
#
# Do not resolve that consequence by copying, vendoring, duplicating, exposing or otherwise
# exporting shared platform source. Broadening this manifest to satisfy an import is
# explicitly forbidden.
#
# ENFORCEMENT GAP, verified 2026-09-02: A-2's stage-2 protected-class check does NOT
# mechanically reject ordinary shared platform source -- such source is not a secret, not
# training material and not runtime state, so it passes stage 2 unflagged. Protection against
# exporting shared-but-unprotected platform source therefore rests on the discipline of this
# manifest and on review. No mechanical ownership guard exists, and building one was
# deliberately excluded from A-4; it is tracked as a separate open decision.
#
# Also absent, each for its own reason:
#   tests                     not part of the deliverable under this ruling (Option C refused)
#   run/                      runtime state; the exporter refuses it at stage 2 regardless
#   ops/ reverse-proxy conf   internal infrastructure configuration
#   tools/ provisioning CLI   operator tooling, and the sole entitlement writer
#   archives/ prior exports   self-labelled internal-only; contain infrastructure config
#   __pycache__, .pytest_cache  build artefacts, not source
#
# One path per line, repo-relative. Blank lines and # comments ignored.

# --- the customer-facing page -------------------------------------------------------
backend/apps/dispatchos/page.py

# --- application-specific source ----------------------------------------------------
backend/apps/dispatchos/__init__.py
backend/apps/dispatchos/routes.py
backend/apps/dispatchos/store.py
backend/apps/dispatchos/quotes.py
backend/apps/dispatchos/ai.py
backend/apps/dispatchos/authz.py
